**DEDUCED — `regress/artifacts/xscaleinten/codex_pass2_20260911.txt`.**
Codex predicted **26/26** for `M_OPCODE1` on the old witness; this was never a measured escape
in the supplied SCORES files. Every tested inten access used `opcode1=0`; `E_UNKNOWN` tested
nonzero opcode1 at a rejected register tuple. Calling that cell disclosed was wrong.
Opcode fields are inputs ignored by this handler, not its dispatch guards.
The pass endorsed the deletion and identified missing opcode1, isteer-preservation and isolated
crm coverage. `D_TRR0` changed crm and crn together. The promoted table measures the replacement
rows below; it does not retroactively measure the predicted old-instrument escape.

